{
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "strings": {
    "A second shortcut that shows only the frontmost app's windows. Off by default — the usual ⌘` is a shortcut apps use themselves.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A second shortcut that shows only the frontmost app's windows. Off by default — the usual ⌘` is a shortcut apps use themselves."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Un second raccourci qui n'affiche que les fenêtres de l'application au premier plan. Désactivé par défaut — le ⌘` habituel est un raccourci que les applications utilisent elles-mêmes."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A theme carries only the look — never a shortcut — so importing one can not change what your keys do.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A theme carries only the look — never a shortcut — so importing one can not change what your keys do."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Un thème ne contient que l'apparence — jamais un raccourci — donc en importer un ne peut pas changer ce que font vos touches."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A twentieth of the screen at a time, from the middle of the window outward, stopping at the edges.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A twentieth of the screen at a time, from the middle of the window outward, stopping at the edges."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Un vingtième de l'écran à la fois, depuis le centre de la fenêtre vers l'extérieur, en s'arrêtant aux bords."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "About": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "About"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "À propos"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Accessibility": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Accessibility"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Accessibilité"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Accessibility is granted per binary. A rebuild signed with a different certificate looks like a new app to macOS and has to be granted again.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Accessibility is granted per binary. A rebuild signed with a different certificate looks like a new app to macOS and has to be granted again."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "L'accessibilité est accordée par binaire. Une nouvelle compilation signée avec un autre certificat ressemble à une nouvelle application pour macOS et doit être autorisée à nouveau."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Act on the highlighted tile without leaving the switcher. Each is a key plus ⌥ or ⌃ held on top of the trigger — an extra modifier is required, since a bare letter is type-to-filter input.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Act on the highlighted tile without leaving the switcher. Each is a key plus ⌥ or ⌃ held on top of the trigger — an extra modifier is required, since a bare letter is type-to-filter input."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Agissez sur la vignette sélectionnée sans quitter le sélecteur. Chaque action est une touche plus ⌥ ou ⌃ maintenue en plus du déclencheur — un modificateur supplémentaire est obligatoire, car une lettre seule sert à filtrer."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "All desktops": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "All desktops"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tous les bureaux"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "All windows": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "All windows"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Toutes les fenêtres"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Almost maximize": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Almost maximize"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Presque plein écran"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Alphabetical order always groups: sorted by name, an ungrouped list would scatter one app's windows wherever the alphabet put them.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Alphabetical order always groups: sorted by name, an ungrouped list would scatter one app's windows wherever the alphabet put them."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "L'ordre alphabétique groupe toujours : triée par nom, une liste non groupée disperserait les fenêtres d'une application au gré de l'alphabet."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Also reachable by pressing the matching half twice or three times — this is the same place in one press.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Also reachable by pressing the matching half twice or three times — this is the same place in one press."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Également accessible en appuyant deux ou trois fois sur la moitié correspondante — ceci y mène en une seule pression."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An exported file carries every preference, including favourites and exclusions.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An exported file carries every preference, including favourites and exclusions."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Un fichier exporté contient tous les réglages, favoris et exclusions compris."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Anchor dot": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Anchor dot"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Point d'ancrage"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "App rules": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "App rules"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Règles par application"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Appearance": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Appearance"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Apparence"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Application mode only — a window list has as many tiles per app as the app has windows, so no app can hold a slot in it.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Application mode only — a window list has as many tiles per app as the app has windows, so no app can hold a slot in it."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Mode application uniquement — une liste de fenêtres contient autant de vignettes par application que celle-ci a de fenêtres, donc aucune application ne peut y garder une place."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Apps": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Apps"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Applications"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ask first for Quit and Force-quit. One key separates ⌥W (close a window) from ⌥Q (quit the app), and only one of them can be undone.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ask first for Quit and Force-quit. One key separates ⌥W (close a window) from ⌥Q (quit the app), and only one of them can be undone."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Demander confirmation pour Quitter et Forcer à quitter. Une seule touche sépare ⌥W (fermer une fenêtre) de ⌥Q (quitter l'application), et une seule des deux est réversible."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Backup": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Backup"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Sauvegarde"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Behavior": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Behavior"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Comportement"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bindings are matched in the order listed above, so the first one to claim a combination is the one that fires. Openers come first: nothing you bind can take the switcher's own trigger away from it.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bindings are matched in the order listed above, so the first one to claim a combination is the one that fires. Openers come first: nothing you bind can take the switcher's own trigger away from it."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Les raccourcis sont évalués dans l'ordre ci-dessus : le premier à revendiquer une combinaison est celui qui se déclenche. Les ouvertures passent en premier — rien de ce que vous associez ne peut retirer au sélecteur son propre déclencheur."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bottom half": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bottom half"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
