    "Move your whole setup between Macs.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Move your whole setup between Macs."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Emportez toute votre configuration d'un Mac à l'autre."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Moves the keyboard to the nearest window in that direction — the other half of tiling, which places windows but never let you walk between them. Live whether or not tiling is on, since focus resizes nothing. Unbound by default: every arrow combination on ⌃⌘ is already spoken for, and the only one left is ⌃⌥⇧⌘, which is not a chord to claim on your behalf.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Moves the keyboard to the nearest window in that direction — the other half of tiling, which places windows but never let you walk between them. Live whether or not tiling is on, since focus resizes nothing. Unbound by default: every arrow combination on ⌃⌘ is already spoken for, and the only one left is ⌃⌥⇧⌘, which is not a chord to claim on your behalf."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Amène le clavier sur la fenêtre la plus proche dans cette direction — l'autre moitié du pavage, qui plaçait les fenêtres sans jamais vous laisser circuler entre elles. Actif que le pavage soit activé ou non, puisque le focus ne redimensionne rien. Non associé par défaut : toutes les combinaisons de flèches sur ⌃⌘ sont déjà prises, et la seule restante est ⌃⌥⇧⌘, qui n'est pas un raccourci à revendiquer à votre place."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Moves the window without resizing it, a twentieth of the screen a press. Stops at the screen edge rather than walking the window off it.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Moves the window without resizing it, a twentieth of the screen a press. Stops at the screen edge rather than walking the window off it."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Déplace la fenêtre sans la redimensionner, d'un vingtième de l'écran par pression. S'arrête au bord de l'écran plutôt que d'y faire sortir la fenêtre."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Names the destination instead of counting to it: on three displays \"next display\" is two presses and a guess about which way round they are, where these land on the same screen every time. The numbers are the ones on the window tiles' own display badges. Unbound, and ungoverned by the tiling switch for the same reason the two moves above are. Rows appear for the displays you actually have.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Names the destination instead of counting to it: on three displays \"next display\" is two presses and a guess about which way round they are, where these land on the same screen every time. The numbers are the ones on the window tiles' own display badges. Unbound, and ungoverned by the tiling switch for the same reason the two moves above are. Rows appear for the displays you actually have."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Nomme la destination au lieu de la compter : sur trois écrans, « écran suivant » demande deux pressions et une supposition sur leur ordre, alors que ceux-ci arrivent sur le même écran à chaque fois. Les numéros sont ceux des pastilles d'écran portées par les vignettes de fenêtre. Non associés, et non régis par l'interrupteur de pavage pour la même raison que les deux déplacements ci-dessus. Les lignes n'apparaissent que pour les écrans dont vous disposez réellement."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "No conflicts": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
