      }
    },
    "The shape the switcher takes.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The shape the switcher takes."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "La forme que prend le sélecteur."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The takeover lives in the window server's memory, never in `com.apple.symbolichotkeys`, so logging out restores ⌘-Tab too.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The takeover lives in the window server's memory, never in `com.apple.symbolichotkeys`, so logging out restores ⌘-Tab too."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "La prise de contrôle réside dans la mémoire du serveur de fenêtres, jamais dans `com.apple.symbolichotkeys` : fermer la session rétablit donc aussi ⌘-Tab."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The two moves keep the window's size and its relative position on the new display, and are live whether or not tiling is on: a move changes no layout, so the switch above does not govern it, and a bound chord is claimed system-wide. The two switches below them are about what happens around a display change rather than about the chords.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The two moves keep the window's size and its relative position on the new display, and are live whether or not tiling is on: a move changes no layout, so the switch above does not govern it, and a bound chord is claimed system-wide. The two switches below them are about what happens around a display change rather than about the chords."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Les deux déplacements conservent la taille de la fenêtre et sa position relative sur le nouvel écran, et sont actifs que le pavage soit activé ou non : un déplacement ne change aucune disposition, donc l'interrupteur ci-dessus ne le régit pas, et un raccourci associé est revendiqué pour tout le système. Les deux interrupteurs en dessous concernent ce qui se passe autour d'un changement d'écrans, pas les raccourcis."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The two windows change places, each taking the other's exact frame.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The two windows change places, each taking the other's exact frame."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Les deux fenêtres échangent leur place, chacune prenant le cadre exact de l'autre."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The ⌘-number jump hint on the first ten targets.": {
