    },
    "Windows": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Windows"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Fenêtres"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Windows on this desktop": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Windows on this desktop"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Les fenêtres de ce bureau"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Windows on this display": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Windows on this display"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Les fenêtres de cet écran"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Written in place rather than replaced, so a symlink into a dotfiles repo survives every save. On launch the file wins over local settings — that is what makes a fresh checkout come up configured, and what makes a second Mac pick up the settings iCloud sent it rather than publish its own over them.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Written in place rather than replaced, so a symlink into a dotfiles repo survives every save. On launch the file wins over local settings — that is what makes a fresh checkout come up configured, and what makes a second Mac pick up the settings iCloud sent it rather than publish its own over them."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Écrit sur place plutôt que remplacé, pour qu'un lien symbolique vers un dépôt de dotfiles survive à chaque enregistrement. Au lancement, le fichier l'emporte sur les réglages locaux — c'est ce qui fait qu'un dépôt fraîchement cloné démarre configuré, et qu'un second Mac reprend les réglages qu'iCloud lui a envoyés au lieu d'imposer les siens."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Zoom window": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Zoom window"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Zoomer la fenêtre"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "macOS has no way to move another app's window between desktops, so this performs the gesture instead: it picks the window up, opens Mission Control for a moment and drops it on the next desktop along. That means it takes over the pointer for about half a second, which is why it is off by default. Stops at the first and last desktop rather than wrapping around.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "macOS has no way to move another app's window between desktops, so this performs the gesture instead: it picks the window up, opens Mission Control for a moment and drops it on the next desktop along. That means it takes over the pointer for about half a second, which is why it is off by default. Stops at the first and last desktop rather than wrapping around."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "macOS n'offre aucun moyen de déplacer la fenêtre d'une autre application entre les bureaux : ceci exécute donc le geste à la main — la fenêtre est saisie, Mission Control s'ouvre un instant, et elle est déposée sur le bureau suivant. Cela mobilise le pointeur pendant environ une demi-seconde, d'où sa désactivation par défaut. S'arrête au premier et au dernier bureau au lieu de boucler."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "macOS raises a window as part of focusing it, so the window you rest over comes to the front. Nothing happens while a mouse button or a modifier is held, or while the switcher is open — each of those is a gesture that belongs to the window it started in.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "macOS raises a window as part of focusing it, so the window you rest over comes to the front. Nothing happens while a mouse button or a modifier is held, or while the switcher is open — each of those is a gesture that belongs to the window it started in."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "macOS met une fenêtre au premier plan en même temps qu'il l'active : celle que vous survolez passe donc devant. Rien ne se produit tant qu'un bouton de la souris ou un modificateur est maintenu, ni pendant que le sélecteur est ouvert — chacun de ces cas est un geste qui appartient à la fenêtre où il a commencé."
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "version": "1.0"
}
